  caseId: 1
  title: The Missing Keris
  briefing: Yesterday evening, an antique keris disappeared from its display case
    in the Heritage Gallery's Melaka Room, one week before it was due to go on loan
    overseas. The case was found open this morning. Four people had a reason to be
    near the room last night. Search the room, tag the evidence, and name the person
    who took the keris.
  suspects:
  - id: Y_farid
    displayName: Farid Rahman
    role: Tour guide
    alibi: '"My last tour ended at 7:30 pm and I went home." (No one can confirm.)'
  - id: Y_tan
    displayName: Mr Tan
    role: Security guard
    alibi: On gate duty 8:00-9:00 pm; the front-desk camera shows him there.
  - id: Y_sofia
    displayName: Dr Sofia Idris
    role: Curator
    alibi: Hosting a donor dinner across town 7:00-9:30 pm; the guests confirm it.
  - id: Y_lim
    displayName: Mr Lim
    role: Private collector
    alibi: On a flight that landed at KLIA at 9:00 pm; the airline confirms it.
  correctSuspectId: Y_farid
  keyEvidenceIds:
  - Y_K1
  - Y_K2
  - Y_K3
  - Y_K4
  experimenterNotes: 'Generated from docs/cases.md by FYP > Build Case Scenes.

    Culprit:
    Farid Rahman

    K1 Y_K1 - Display case alarm panel

    K2 Y_K2 - Key logbook

    K3
    Y_K3 - Laser pointer

    K4 Y_K4 - Printed chat message

    R1 Y_R1 - Torch
    (red herring: Mr Tan)

    R2 Y_R2 - Business card (red herring: Mr Lim)

    R3
    Y_R3 - Noticeboard note (red herring: Dr Sofia Idris)

'
